    "result_text": "Done. The full build succeeds with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag on the owner response, mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` design and reusing the city-capacity logic rather than duplicating it.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `capacityWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the code generator emits `getCapacityWarning`/`setCapacityWarning` on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **New `CityCapacityWarningEvaluator`** (`rest/validation`) \u2014 A small single-responsibility component that answers \"is this city approaching capacity?\". It uses `ClinicService.countOwnersInCity(...)` and returns true when the count is in `[40, 50)` \u2014 reusing `CityOwnerLimitValidator.MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` as the upper bound so the warning band and the hard limit stay in lockstep. I placed it alongside `CityOwnerLimitValidator` precisely so it can share that constant.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.toOwnerDto(...)`** \u2014 Now also stamps `capacityWarning` onto the DTO via the new evaluator, keeping the single place where per-response warnings are attached.\n\nThe hard rejection at 50 (`CityOwnerLimitValidator`) is untouched. The acceptance test (`coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` \u2014 fill a city to 40, create one more, expect `capacityWarning: true`) passes, as does the full suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
